@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Resolve a reconciliation discrepancy — End-to-end interaction
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Accommodation Provider Agent" as Actor
participant "Provider Portal / PMS" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Provider Integration Adapter" as Edge
participant "Accommodation Reconciliation Service" as Service1
participant "Provider Billing Service" as Service2
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events
participant "Booking.com Demand API" as BookingCom #FBDADD
participant "Existing ESB / enterprise system" as Enterprise #DDE1F6

group 1. Compare internal events, supplier orders, invoices, and payments.
  Actor -> Surface: Compare internal events, supplier orders, invoices, and payments
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/reconciliation/cases/{caseId}/evidence
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Compare internal events, supplier orders, invoices, and payments.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> BookingCom: orders/details and existing finance integrations
  BookingCom --> Service1: Supplier response + request_id
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Supply correction or evidence for a reconciliation discrepancy.
  Actor -> Surface: Supply correction or evidence for a reconciliation discrepancy
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /provider-api/v1/reconciliation/{caseId}/responses
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service2: Supply correction or evidence for a reconciliation discrepancy.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service2 -> Service2: Validate transition and persist
  Service2 -> Data: Read or commit Provider Billing Service data
  Service2 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service2 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service2 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
